## fastcompile-macros 8: codegen: a root that is a generic instance, for the compiled tier of proc macros

Where: `crates/hir-ty-codegen/v2/frontend.rs`, beside `HirFrontend::root`.

Why: the compiled tier (`crates/blaze-macro-eval/src/tier/`, change 20) reaches a macro crate from each macro's client, `proc_macro::bridge::client::Client::expand1::<F>` / `expand2::<F>` with `F` the fn item type of the `#[proc_macro*]` function, as the evaluator calls them (`blaze-macro-eval/src/run.rs` `on_evaluator`). `root` takes only a non-generic function, and the `__blaze_proc_macros` static macros-tier.md meant to root from is not in the daemon's front end (nor should it be: request fastcompile-macros 7 stops building proc-macro units natively).

What, the narrowest entry, costing nothing unused:

```rust
/// The instance of `func` whose type parameters are, in order, the fn item types of `items`
/// (no lifetimes, no consts): a root of the compiled tier of proc macros. An error names
/// `func` when its generics are not that many type parameters.
pub fn root_with_fn_items(&self, func: FunctionId, items: &[FunctionId]) -> Result<HirInstance, CodegenError>;
```

Built as `root_in` builds a root, with one `GenericArg` of `Ty::new_fn_def(interner, CallableDefId::FunctionId(item).into(), GenericArgs::default())` per item (run.rs ~line 380 builds the same arguments for the evaluator).
